========================================================================================
READING FOR THE LRC(14) PROOF ROUTE
========================================================================================
1. The support-floor sequence is the hard cancellation: all lower support faces vanish, so boundary/cusp mass must be read through six-fold residues.
2. The residue constants decay with ambient dimension, but coordinate marginals stay nonzero; the proof object is the signed coimage over sum e_i n_i=0, not a product of one-coordinate cancellations.
3. The S12 cusp ratio sequence shows why absolute Minkowski volume is the wrong measure.  The integer relation counts are huge exactly where the signed reciprocal mass is tiny.
4. The center-survivor and empty-window sequences are the companion finite spines.  They say which runner-count regimes need a high-degree local certificate, and which small-speed residues pass to colored recurrence.
5. LRC(14) remains open.  The sharpened sub-problem is a tail theorem for residue-addressed reciprocal sums after low-height wall deletion.
